{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Issue #606 and ADR 0021 require Workspaces to reach ACP Sessions through an MCP gateway, with current attachment, effective status, permission, and tool membership authorization. The ACP backend passed no MCP server, and Workspace invocation requests carried no Timeline identity or permission result.","decision":"Add a session-scoped authenticated loopback MCP HTTP server to the ACP backend. Build tools dynamically from attached Workspaces; recheck status, membership, attachment, and permission at call time. Carry the Timeline and approved permission bit through remote invocation so the Workspace-owning Node can fail closed. Require a Timeline ID in the public Workspace client invocation.","impact":"ACP Runtimes advertising HTTP MCP now receive a bearer-authenticated MCP endpoint on new and resumed Sessions, including Sessions that gain Workspaces after startup. Workspace calls work on scratch and local Projects. Additive invocation fields preserve decoding, but GnosticWorkspaceClient.invoke has a new required Timeline argument. No dependency pins changed.","recurrence_control":"Red/green ACP fixture test proves session/new supplies a live authenticated server and the fixture can initialize, list, and call tools; coverage also checks attachment and status changes, runtime attach/detach, owner-node Timeline checks, permission-required calls, and both Project modes. make verify, make acp-smoke, make runner-smoke, and git diff --check passed.","rejected_alternatives":["Treating tools/list as authorization; attachment and status can change after listing.","Forwarding an invocation without Timeline identity or permission state; the Workspace-owning Node could not authorize the call."],"sources":[]}
